# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the GCC ASan+UBSan C++ test leg.
#
# Entries are limited to unavoidable uninstrumented third-party allocations that persist until
# process exit. Never suppress first-party allocations or common frames such as
# `leak:_PyObject_Malloc` and `leak:default_malloc`, which would hide real leaks.
#
# The Python leg disables leak checks: an instrumented extension in stock CPython cannot give
# LSan a clean baseline.

# Open MPI and PMIx retain process state initialized by MPI_Init.
leak:ompi_mpi_init
leak:ompi_mpi_instance_init
leak:ompi_comm_init_mpi3
leak:pmix_hash_fetch
leak:PMIx_Value_create
leak:pmix_bfrops_base_value_load

# Open MPI tears down this libevent base after LSan's exit-time check.
leak:event_base_loop
